 "about_text": "Del Vaz Projects is a nonprofit art space based in Los Angeles, founded in 2014 by Jay Ezra Nayssan in a home-turned-artists space in Santa Monica and accredited as a 501(c)(3) in 2021. The organization mounts exhibitions, produces publications, and stages performance and moving-image programs, often in partnership with museums, foundations, and other Los Angeles institutions. It positions itself as an incubator for artists, archives, and estates, pairing curatorial projects with a research collective and independent press that produce artist books and exhibition catalogs. Its program brings together artists across generations and geographies, with particular attention to underrepresented estates and archives and collaborations across the city's cultural institutions.",
